1. Who owns this work

Copyright in everything in this repository belongs to the people who wrote it: the contributors named above and anyone else whose commits are in its history. Nothing in this file transfers that copyright to INIT or to anyone else.

2. What INIT may do

Each contributor grants INIT a perpetual, irrevocable, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, preserve, archive and display this repository and its history, in INIT Arc and on INIT's own sites. INIT keeps the repository so that the work is not lost. INIT does not use the software, sell it or license it to anyone else.

3. What the team may do

Each contributor grants every other contributor a perpetual, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to use, change and license the team's work in this repository. Any one of them may take the whole project and continue it without asking the others, and none of them may stop the others doing the same.

4. What everyone else may do

No other rights are granted. This repository is public on GitHub, so under GitHub's Terms of Service anyone may view it and fork it on GitHub, and nothing more. Anyone who wants to use the work asks a contributor, who may license their own fork as they choose.

5. After the submission date

From 2 January 2027 to 3 March 2027 the team builds in this repository as part of INIT Studio. After 3 March 2027 INIT preserves it as it stood, and the contributors continue the work in their own forks.

This text is a draft, written without legal advice. INIT may replace it with a later version.
